<Prose title="Privacy" description="What Warble and this website collect, which is nothing.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Last updated 25 October 2026.</p>
  <p>Warble doesn't collect anything about you. It reads what's playing on your Mac so it can show it in the notch, and that information stays on your Mac.</p>
  <p>Warble goes online to check GitHub for updates, and it asks before it does that.</p>
  <p>This website has no cookies or analytics. Cloudflare hosts it and GitHub hosts the downloads, so <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's</a> privacy policies cover those requests.</p>
  <p>Questions go in <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/issues">GitHub issues</a>. For anything private, such as a security problem, use <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/security/advisories/new">GitHub's private reporting</a>. See the <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>.</p>
</Prose>
